{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/257047-making-the-titans-interesting-antagonists","id":257047,"title":"Making the Titans interesting antagonists ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-15T01:22:00-07:00","id":257047,"title":"Making the Titans interesting antagonists ?","content":"So far, the Titans are forces of nature trying to turn the World into whatever element they represent. Surtr wants to burn everything, Mami Wata wants to drown everything, Aten wants to sear everything in light. It's really cool, but it's hard to make them anything other than pure Evil Evilness of Evil Evil. My group once was fighting a bunch of Fire Giants, and tried talking to one, and I realized their interactions with it are pretty restricted - sure, individual Titanspawn could stray from the herd, but still, they usually just mirror the whole &quot;burn everything&quot; ambition. I like more nuanced baddies, with agendas that are incompatible with the ones of the heroes, but make sense in a human logic framework, so that my group has more complex interactions with them than just killing them in the face. <br /> <br /> Anyone encountered this before ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3865-rwandrall","name":"Rwandrall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T05:14:31-07:00","id":257210,"title":"","content":"Yes, I've encountered that before. From what I gathered in reading the books, the Titanspawn have a certain sort of alien-ness to them, and I would describe many of them as text-book sociopaths. Kind of hard to carry on a conversation with something that just cannot grasp concepts beyond &quot;Burninate the fleshie and all his thatch-roofed cottageeeeeeeees.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, when I want a nuanced bad guy, I whip out a Titan-corrupted Scion. Put him in charge of some Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> If I was dead-set on making the Titans or Titanspawn more than one-dimensional bad guys to knock down, then I'd just go ahead and do it. Change the rules on their behaviour to suit my needs accordingly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2789-laume78","name":"laume78","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T06:02:26-07:00","id":257232,"title":"","content":"I prefer the conflict between the Gods and the Titans to be less clear-cut, so I tend to cull the number of Titans and then make the reminder more varied in their opinions. For example, I prefer Prometheus as a Titan-corrupted God rather than a Titan, since Greek Titans aren't the same as Scion Titans. In contrast, I prefer both El and Ahura Mazda as benevolent Titans, while figures such as Shu and Tefnut are either neutral or perhaps even supportive of their pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T12:16:49-07:00","id":257480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rwandrall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/257047-making-the-titans-interesting-antagonists#post257047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, the Titans are forces of nature trying to turn the World into whatever element they represent. Surtr wants to burn everything, Mami Wata wants to drown everything, Aten wants to sear everything in light. It's really cool, but it's hard to make them anything other than pure Evil Evilness of Evil Evil. My group once was fighting a bunch of Fire Giants, and tried talking to one, and I realized their interactions with it are pretty restricted - sure, individual Titanspawn could stray from the herd, but still, they usually just mirror the whole &quot;burn everything&quot; ambition. I like more nuanced baddies, with agendas that are incompatible with the ones of the heroes, but make sense in a human logic framework, so that my group has more complex interactions with them than just killing them in the face.<br /> <br /> Anyone encountered this before ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest problem with Scion 1stED is that the Titans are just evil. That doesn't really give into decent Storytelling (as you pointed out). What I tend to run, and this has worked out amazingly well, is that Titan is a term for a divine being that is ...distant from humanity to the point that humans aren't really on their radar when they're going about their existence.<br /> <br /> Sure, Apep's trying to devour Ra, but he doesn't actually care about the humans scurrying around the world he's going to plunge into darkness. Sure, Chronus devoured his children, but humans were around when he was and they even had a Golden Age under his rule (I'll have to find the sources for that, but it's Zeus that fucks with humanity, not the Titan Generation).<br /> <br /> You can even have Gods within a pantheon that are more 'evil' than the Titans, but because they're invested in humanity to some degree, they're still players in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Now as for Titanspawn, they get to become nuanced if they're human-like. Titanspawn like zombies or what-have-you, sure mindless swarming, but in my Ragnarok Game, Hati and Skoll had taken on the guise of being a Law Firm devoted to shutting down and hindering all Aesir commerce and business within the state of Nevada. They had Fire Giant retainers who served as bouncers and thugs but could be bribed, even, to look the other way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Remove the idea of &quot;Dark Virtues&quot; and &quot;Evil&quot; and turn the Titans into beings that just don't care one way or another about humanity. It still paints them a threat, but a threat that can be approached in more ways than &quot;I smash you in face!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T18:06:57-07:00","id":258596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The biggest problem with Scion 1stED is that the Titans are just evil. That doesn't really give into decent Storytelling (as you pointed out). What I tend to run, and this has worked out amazingly well, is that Titan is a term for a divine being that is ...distant from humanity to the point that humans aren't really on their radar when they're going about their existence.<br /> <br /> Sure, Apep's trying to devour Ra, but he doesn't actually care about the humans scurrying around the world he's going to plunge into darkness. Sure, Chronus devoured his children, but humans were around when he was and they even had a Golden Age under his rule (I'll have to find the sources for that, but it's Zeus that fucks with humanity, not the Titan Generation).<br /> <br /> You can even have Gods within a pantheon that are more 'evil' than the Titans, but because they're invested in humanity to some degree, they're still players in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Now as for Titanspawn, they get to become nuanced if they're human-like. Titanspawn like zombies or what-have-you, sure mindless swarming, but in my Ragnarok Game, Hati and Skoll had taken on the guise of being a Law Firm devoted to shutting down and hindering all Aesir commerce and business within the state of Nevada. They had Fire Giant retainers who served as bouncers and thugs but could be bribed, even, to look the other way.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Remove the idea of &quot;Dark Virtues&quot; and &quot;Evil&quot; and turn the Titans into beings that just don't care one way or another about humanity. It still paints them a threat, but a threat that can be approached in more ways than &quot;I smash you in face!&quot; </div> </div> </div>That seems alot like what I am looking for, would you mind expanding on how this works ? Do Titans still want to shape the World in their image ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3865-rwandrall","name":"Rwandrall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T22:53:55-07:00","id":258750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rwandrall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/257047-making-the-titans-interesting-antagonists?p=258596#post258596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems alot like what I am looking for, would you mind expanding on how this works ? Do Titans still want to shape the World in their image ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Completely depends on the Titan (or Greater Titan Realm in question) and what sort of story I'm wanting to run at the moment. In my Just-About-To-Hit-God game, the Titans are actually not really relelvant? Well, they're being unsealed and causing mischief, but they're not the big bads. In fact, the Greek Titans themselves are being courted by the newly crowned King of Olympus to return to the fold.<br /> <br /> In my baby-hero game, Darkness Falls, it starts off with Apep devouring the sun. Sun's gone, Sun Gods are MIA, and there are defintiely titanspawns causing hell in downtown NYC, but the group hasn't encountered anything beyond what they only know as &quot;Pale Men&quot; and Apep Spawnlings. <br /> <br /> But for expanding on the idea... hmm. It's really hard to say 'this is how'. I guess one of the ways I would suggest is the Dark Virtues thing. Completely seperate them from 'evil'. There are dozens of Gods who should have 'Dark' virtues and some Titans who should have nothing but like 'Order, Harmony, Piety, and Conviction'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T23:33:14-07:00","id":266001,"title":"","content":"Plus, it would depend on what Titans would be considered villians in Second Edition. From what I've read in the developer threads, there are some Titans that might be &quot;good&quot; and probably geared for possible parentage themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T14:59:57-07:00","id":266443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/257047-making-the-titans-interesting-antagonists?p=266001#post266001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, it would depend on what Titans would be considered villians in Second Edition. From what I've read in the developer threads, there are some Titans that might be &quot;good&quot; and probably geared for possible parentage themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes directly back into the problem of &quot;Good&quot; vs. &quot;Evil&quot; is inherantly dull unless you've got some really good motivations on both sides. The OP even stated he was tired of the evil Titans because you can't interact with them beyond RAWRSMASH! and that's a huge flaw with Scion 1stED as it is. If Scion2ED keeps the whole &quot;evil and dark virtues makes a titan... even though we changed the names guys&quot; it's gonna hit that wall again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:24:05-07:00","id":267797,"title":"","content":"Well it's kind of difficult to give a multi-dimensional personality to creatures are are physical embodiments of nature. One might as well tell Galactus to stop eating planets.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ts4.mm.bing.net/th?id=HN.608013485032147091&amp;pid=15.1&amp;P=0\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> In a way, having them be one dimensional has its own side of making them interesting. If the Titans and their spawn are just nature given form, then that means the Scions and their parents are interfering with the course of nature. This actually makes sense, as many creation myths are about the time when humanity first began to impose its will over nature. On a further note, I don't think it's possible for an incarnation of nature to be either good or evil. They're just a law of the cosmos doing what they're supposed to do. Whether it's good or evil is purely speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}